+##### Ear detection (read-only)
+
+Where each bud is, as the headphones report it (packet 0x06) whenever a bud
+is put in or taken out of an ear or put in the case. Listed from the first
+report after connecting; headphones without ear detection never list it.
+`primary` is the bud that holds the link to the host; when it is taken out
+the headphones usually make the other bud primary and report again. `left`
+and `right` are listed once the battery report has said which bud is
+primary. Headphones with one component (AirPods Max) report only `primary`
+meaningfully.
+
+```json
+{
+  "earDetection": {
+    "readonly": true,
+    "primary": "inEar",
+    "secondary": "outOfEar",
+    "left": "inEar",
+    "right": "outOfEar"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+| Value      |                                              |
+| ---------- | -------------------------------------------- |
+| `inEar`    | In an ear                                    |
+| `outOfEar` | Out of the ear, not in the case              |
+| `inCase`   | In the case                                  |
+| `unknown`  | Not connected, or a value this version does not know |
+
+The daemon also pauses the media player that is playing (MPRIS,
+`org.mpris.MediaPlayer2.*` on the session bus) when buds are taken out, and
+resumes the same player when they are back, following the
+`earDetectionPause` setting (see "Daemon settings"). It resumes only a player
+it paused itself, only if that player is still paused, and never after the
+user played or stopped it in the meantime or after the headphones
+disconnected.
+
+
 ### Features that need Apple's Device ID
 
 AirPods offer some features only to hosts whose Device ID (the DID profile)
@@ -1003,5 +1042,15 @@ If any setting changes:
 ```
 
 
+### Daemon settings
 
+The daemon keeps its own settings in the `magicpods` container, read and
+written with the methods above.
 
+| Setting             | Type   | Default        | Meaning |
+| ------------------- | ------ | -------------- | ------- |
+| `earDetectionPause` | string | `"oneRemoved"` | When to pause media as buds leave the ears: `"off"`; `"oneRemoved"`, when any worn bud is taken out (resumed when all of them are back); `"bothRemoved"`, when no bud is left in an ear (resumed when one is back). Any other value means `"oneRemoved"`. Applies from the next change of the buds on. |
+
+```json
+{"method":"SetSetting","arguments":{"container":"magicpods","setting":"earDetectionPause","value":"bothRemoved"}}
+```
